{"results":[{"id":"UP000000425","description":"Gram-negative meningococcal bacterium. Neisseria meningitidis colonizes the mucosal surface of the human nose and throat, usually as a commensal bacterium. Up to 15% of the human population are asymptomatic carriers. Sometimes the strains can invade the host, causing life-threatening invasive bacterial infections especially in young infants. They do so by gaining access to the blood and to the cerebrospinal fluid to cause meningitis and septicemia. Thus it is a major cause of morbidity and mortality. The pattern of serogroup B disease is typically hyperendemic or sporadic. Strains of this serogroup are a particular problem because they are a major cause of invasive disease in Europe and United States and there is currently no effective vaccine.","taxonomy":{"scientificName":"Neisseria meningitidis serogroup B (strain ATCC BAA-335 / MC58)","taxonId":122586,"mnemonic":"NEIMB"},"modified":"2026-07-07","proteomeType":"Reference proteome","strain":"ATCC BAA-335 / MC58","components":[{"name":"Chromosome","description":"Neisseria meningitidis MC58, complete genome.","proteinCount":2003,"genomeAnnotation":{"source":"ENA/EMBL"},"proteomeCrossReferences":[{"database":"GenomeAccession","id":"AE002098"},{"database":"Biosample","id":"SAMN02603997"}]}],"citations":[{"id":"10710307","citationType":"journal article","authors":["Tettelin H.","Saunders N.J.","Heidelberg J.F.","Jeffries A.C.","Nelson K.E.","Eisen J.A.","Ketchum K.A.","Hood D.W.","Peden J.F.","Dodson R.J.","Nelson W.C.","Gwinn M.L.","DeBoy R.T.","Peterson J.D.","Hickey E.K.","Haft D.H.","Salzberg S.L.","White O.","Fleischmann R.D.","Dougherty B.A.","Mason T.M.","Ciecko A.","Parksey D.S.","Blair E.","Cittone H.","Clark E.B.","Cotton M.D.","Utterback T.R.","Khouri H.M.","Qin H.","Vamathevan J.J.","Gill J.","Scarlato V.","Masignani V.","Pizza M.","Grandi G.","Sun L.","Smith H.O.","Fraser C.M.","Moxon E.R.","Rappuoli R.","Venter J.C."],"citationCrossReferences":[{"database":"PubMed","id":"10710307"},{"database":"DOI","id":"10.1126/science.287.5459.1809"}],"title":"Complete genome sequence of Neisseria meningitidis serogroup B strain MC58.","publicationDate":"2000","journal":"Science","firstPage":"1809","lastPage":"1815","volume":"287"}],"annotationScore":2,"superkingdom":"bacteria","proteomeCompletenessReport":{"buscoReport":{"complete":788,"completeSingle":774,"completeDuplicated":14,"fragmented":2,"missing":14,"total":804,"lineageDb":"neisseriales_odb10","score":98},"cpdReport":{"proteomeCount":2714,"stdCdss":0.0,"averageCdss":0,"confidence":0,"status":"Standard"}},"genomeAssembly":{"assemblyId":"GCA_000008805.1","genomeAssemblyUrl":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ena/browser/view/GCA_000008805.1","level":"full","source":"ENA/EMBL"},"geneCount":2003,"proteinCount":2003,"genomeAnnotation":{"source":"ENA/EMBL","url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ena/browser/view/GCA_000008805.1"},"taxonLineage":[{"scientificName":"cellular organisms","taxonId":131567,"rank":"no rank","hidden":true},{"scientificName":"Bacteria","commonName":"bacteria","taxonId":2,"rank":"domain","hidden":false},{"scientificName":"Pseudomonadati","taxonId":3379134,"rank":"kingdom","hidden":false},{"scientificName":"Pseudomonadota","commonName":"proteobacteria","taxonId":1224,"rank":"phylum","hidden":false},{"scientificName":"Betaproteobacteria","commonName":"b-proteobacteria","taxonId":28216,"rank":"class","hidden":false},{"scientificName":"Neisseriales","taxonId":206351,"rank":"order","hidden":false},{"scientificName":"Neisseriaceae","taxonId":481,"rank":"family","hidden":false},{"scientificName":"Neisseria","taxonId":482,"rank":"genus","hidden":false},{"scientificName":"Neisseria meningitidis","taxonId":487,"rank":"species","hidden":true},{"scientificName":"Neisseria meningitidis serogroup B","taxonId":491,"rank":"serogroup","hidden":true}],"proteomeStatistics":{"reviewedProteinCount":592,"unreviewedProteinCount":1411,"isoformProteinCount":0},"panproteomeTaxon":{"taxonId":487}},{"id":"UP000000535","description":"Neisseria gonorrhoeae is the causative agent of gonorrhea which is a sexually transmitted disease of worldwide importance. It typically infects the mucous membranes causing infections such as urethritis, cervicitis, salpingitis, pelvic inflammatory disease, proctitis, conjunctivitis and pharyngitis. Gonorrhea can also be spread from mother to baby during delivery. This can cause blindness, joint infection, or a life-threatening blood infection in the infant.","taxonomy":{"scientificName":"Neisseria gonorrhoeae (strain ATCC 700825 / FA 1090)","taxonId":242231,"mnemonic":"NEIG1"},"modified":"2026-07-07","proteomeType":"Reference proteome","strain":"ATCC 700825 / FA 1090","components":[{"name":"Chromosome","description":"Neisseria gonorrhoeae FA 1090, complete genome.","proteinCount":2106,"genomeAnnotation":{"source":"ENA/EMBL"},"proteomeCrossReferences":[{"database":"GenomeAccession","id":"AE004969"},{"database":"Biosample","id":"SAMN02604088"}]}],"citations":[{"id":"CI-92V2JQAJ25B4S","citationType":"submission","authors":["Lewis L.A.","Gillaspy A.F.","McLaughlin R.E.","Gipson M.","Ducey T.F.","Ownbey T.","Hartman K.","Nydick C.","Carson M.B.","Vaughn J.","Thomson C.","Song L.","Lin S.","Yuan X.","Najar F.","Zhan M.","Ren Q.","Zhu H.","Qi S.","Kenton S.M.","Lai H.","White J.D.","Clifton S.","Roe B.A.","Dyer D.W."],"title":"The complete genome sequence of Neisseria gonorrhoeae.","publicationDate":"MAR-2003","submissionDatabase":"EMBL/GenBank/DDBJ databases"}],"annotationScore":2,"superkingdom":"bacteria","proteomeCompletenessReport":{"buscoReport":{"complete":785,"completeSingle":785,"completeDuplicated":0,"fragmented":3,"missing":16,"total":804,"lineageDb":"neisseriales_odb10","score":98},"cpdReport":{"proteomeCount":2714,"stdCdss":0.0,"averageCdss":0,"confidence":0,"status":"Close to standard (high value)"}},"genomeAssembly":{"assemblyId":"GCA_000006845.1","genomeAssemblyUrl":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ena/browser/view/GCA_000006845.1","level":"full","source":"ENA/EMBL"},"geneCount":2106,"proteinCount":2106,"genomeAnnotation":{"source":"ENA/EMBL","url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ena/browser/view/GCA_000006845.1"},"taxonLineage":[{"scientificName":"cellular organisms","taxonId":131567,"rank":"no rank","hidden":true},{"scientificName":"Bacteria","commonName":"bacteria","taxonId":2,"rank":"domain","hidden":false},{"scientificName":"Pseudomonadati","taxonId":3379134,"rank":"kingdom","hidden":false},{"scientificName":"Pseudomonadota","commonName":"proteobacteria","taxonId":1224,"rank":"phylum","hidden":false},{"scientificName":"Betaproteobacteria","commonName":"b-proteobacteria","taxonId":28216,"rank":"class","hidden":false},{"scientificName":"Neisseriales","taxonId":206351,"rank":"order","hidden":false},{"scientificName":"Neisseriaceae","taxonId":481,"rank":"family","hidden":false},{"scientificName":"Neisseria","taxonId":482,"rank":"genus","hidden":false},{"scientificName":"Neisseria gonorrhoeae","taxonId":485,"rank":"species","hidden":true}],"proteomeStatistics":{"reviewedProteinCount":430,"unreviewedProteinCount":1676,"isoformProteinCount":0},"panproteomeTaxon":{"taxonId":485},"relatedProteomes":[{"proteomeId":"UP000002564","similarity":0.839,"taxonomy":{"taxonId":521006}},{"proteomeId":"UP001163151","similarity":0.818,"taxonomy":{"taxonId":485}}]},{"id":"UP000002564","description":"Neisseria gonorrhoeae is one of two pathogenic Neisseria, this species causes the sexually transmitted disease (STD) gonorrhea, which is the leading reportable STD in adults in the USA. This human-specific organism colonizes and invades the mucosal surface of the urogenital epithelium, crosses the epithelial barrier, and ends up multiplying on the basement membrane. The result is severe painful inflammation and purulent discharge. Neisseria gonorrhoeae (strain NCCP11945) was isolated in 2002 from a vaginal smear of a Korean patient. This is a multidrug-resistant strain and will be used to understand the prevalence, antibiotic resistance, and importance of horizontal gene transfer within this important, naturally competent organism.","taxonomy":{"scientificName":"Neisseria gonorrhoeae (strain NCCP11945)","taxonId":521006,"mnemonic":"NEIG2"},"modified":"2026-07-07","proteomeType":"Reference proteome","strain":"NCCP11945","components":[{"name":"Chromosome","description":"Neisseria gonorrhoeae NCCP11945, complete genome.","proteinCount":2583,"genomeAnnotation":{"source":"ENA/EMBL"},"proteomeCrossReferences":[{"database":"GenomeAccession","id":"CP001050"},{"database":"Biosample","id":"SAMN02603475"}]},{"name":"Plasmid pNGK","description":"Neisseria gonorrhoeae NCCP11945 plasmid pNGK, complete sequence.","proteinCount":12,"genomeAnnotation":{"source":"ENA/EMBL"},"proteomeCrossReferences":[{"database":"GenomeAccession","id":"CP001051"},{"database":"Biosample","id":"SAMN02603475"}]}],"citations":[{"id":"18586945","citationType":"journal article","authors":["Chung G.T.","Yoo J.S.","Oh H.B.","Lee Y.S.","Cha S.H.","Kim S.J.","Yoo C.K."],"citationCrossReferences":[{"database":"PubMed","id":"18586945"},{"database":"DOI","id":"10.1128/jb.00566-08"}],"title":"Complete genome sequence of Neisseria gonorrhoeae NCCP11945.","publicationDate":"2008","journal":"J. Bacteriol.","firstPage":"6035","lastPage":"6036","volume":"190"}],"annotationScore":2,"superkingdom":"bacteria","proteomeCompletenessReport":{"buscoReport":{"complete":780,"completeSingle":780,"completeDuplicated":0,"fragmented":6,"missing":18,"total":804,"lineageDb":"neisseriales_odb10 (2021-02-23)","score":97},"cpdReport":{"proteomeCount":2714,"stdCdss":0.0,"averageCdss":0,"confidence":0,"status":"Outlier (high value)"}},"genomeAssembly":{"assemblyId":"GCA_000020105.1","genomeAssemblyUrl":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ena/browser/view/GCA_000020105.1","level":"full","source":"ENA/EMBL"},"geneCount":2595,"proteinCount":2595,"genomeAnnotation":{"source":"ENA/EMBL","url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ena/browser/view/GCA_000020105.1"},"taxonLineage":[{"scientificName":